@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.integration"

Feature:  Dossiera To Koroneiki and Okta Integration
	Testing to assure dossiera to koroneiki and okta integration works properly.

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Oktpro - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Prookt - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| PROOKTOKTPRO |
	| PROOKT       |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Oktpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Prookt - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| PROOKTOKTPRO |
	| PROOKT       |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Oktpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Prookt - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| okta.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| okta.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| okta.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| okta.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| okta.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| okta.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| okta.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| okta.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| okta.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| okta.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| okta.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| okta.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Oktpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Prookt - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Create entities with deactivated users
	Testing the ability to create a project in Dossiera and verifying that the respective entities get sent to and created in Koroneiki while deactivated users are not created

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | okta.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | okta.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OKTA                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                            |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | okta.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | okta.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OKTA                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                            |
	And I deactivate the user with the email address "okta.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" from okta
	And I deactivate the user with the email address "okta.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" from okta
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Prookt - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | okta.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken      |
	| Contact First Name                     | OKTA                                       |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | okta.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken      |
	| Owner First Name                       | OKTA                                       |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Oktpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "Oktpro - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Code                  | PROOKTOKTPRO                          | |
	| Parent Account Name   | Prookt - ${staticCompanyName}         | |
	| Contact Email Address | okta.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Name                  | Oktpro - ${staticProjectName}         | |
	| Region                | United States                         | |
	| Status                | Active                                | |
	And I should be able to view a postal address on koroneiki for the account "Oktpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the street address "456 Fake Street" with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 456 Fake Street |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraAccountKey}" and domain "salesforce" should be present on the account "Oktpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraProjectKey}" and domain "dossiera" should be present on the account "Oktpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey} |
	| Entity Name | project                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticSalesforceProjectKey}" should be present on the account "Oktpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} |
	| Entity Name | project                       |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraAccountKey}" and domain "salesforce" should be present on the account "Prookt - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticDossieraAccountKey}" and domain "dossiera" should be present on the account "Prookt - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}" should be present on the product purchase made by account "Oktpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                        |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey} |
	| Entity Name | opportunity                       |
	And the external link with the entity id "${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}" should be present on the product purchase made by account "Oktpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                        |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey} |
	| Entity Name | opportunity                       |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "okta.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "okta.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Oktpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Oktpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |